# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/s7 window (the ship-7 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/s7 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the two runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW AND THE SHIP: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s7-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft and the ship-7 profile baked as the serving default
# (sed -i 's/tp4-s7-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the same in every
# smoke and prefix job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint.
# B0 (STOP): the WINDOW AND SHIP image tp4-s7-1, built from the pushed tp4/s7c head (the ship-6 stack plus the three groups of levers, each default off in its code) with
# the ship-7 candidate c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s7 baked as the serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP baked
# as its max-num-seqs (8), plus C2_BAKE_GRAFT=K64j-OQ. REFUSED by c2_serving_job.read_bake and by build-c2-serving-image.sh while the profile's owner_traffic_waiver has a
# decision that does not start with APPROVED: the owner's approval (conditional on this window's gates) is committed first (make_fusion_profiles.py --approve-ship --ship
# traffic-s7), the CPU suite runs on that commit and the tag is pushed on THAT commit. The control c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s6 is a profile
# of the file chosen by a job's C2_PROFILE, so one image serves both arms of every pair. READ: "baking the serving default
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s7 with a session cap of 8", the provenance report with no problem line ("(c) the image default is the BAKED
# profile ..."), its K64j-OQ graft line, the image id. A build, not a card job: it may run while production serves; no privileged builder container may be up and no card
# job may run during it. Estimate from the last builds: 35-40 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s7-1
C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s7
C2_BAKE_GRAFT=K64j-OQ
